    "turn_text": "But you know, you don't need to worry about that. Yesterday I posted on social media and was greeted with a little bit of consternation. Not as much as I thought though. Not as much as I thought. I said that, you know, if you believe that the IRS is that you have nothing to worry about, about 87,000 new IRS agents, then that's kind of like, I don't know, the German army telling people in the German people that you have nothing to worry about as long as you're not hiding Jews. And I know there was, oh my God, you can't believe you use that, oh my God, oh my God. Well, no, I don't do these things to stir things up. I make honest analogies about what I've seen and how history repeats itself. The IRS wants to go after people who have not done anything wrong. They want to assume guilt and you have to prove that you're not guilty. That's the way the IRS works. And the tax code is so ungodly complicated that one slip on one line could result in ruining you. And that's what they're looking for. There's no other reason for the the IRS to want to hire 87,000 new employees, new enforcement agents when 4% of the money is going to customer service. The rest, a good share of it, 60% is going for enforcement. And they even pull down an ad online looking for IRS agents who know how to handle firearms and would be willing to use deadly force if necessary. That's real. Let's go to Ken and Jessa Maryland. Hello there. Ken, welcome to the Rob Carson show your thoughts today. Please.",
