    "turn_idx": 414,
    "turn_text": "Representative, I mean, you look at all of the other indignities that have been severed upon us. You look at the Afghanistan withdrawal. We saw the president claim some sort of victory with the assassination of Al-Zawahiri, who was openly living in a palatial estate in the country where we abandoned freedom, loving people and left $85 billion in military hardware. We've got that. We've got the open border, the southern border. It is an insult to us to see what's happening. We've had 107,000 people die of overdoses last year. And this is intentional murder by the Chinese government because this fentanyl is disguised as prescription meds and people if they're out of maybe their ADD meds or whatever they'll go on Facebook they will find someone who can give them a pill or two and frequently these pills are are contaminated with fentanyl and they're dying not because they're drug addicts but they're being murdered There are so many things that are going on right now, sir. And the biggest concern we have is we know what we want to do in November, but who's going to stop us? Who's going to try and stop us from doing what free countries do? And that is changing the course of the country with our vote. What assurances can you give the American people that it won't be taken from us?",
